011453000,"application_start_time":1775805638000,"additional_information":"Performannce Architect Intern :&#10;<div>&#10;</div><div>&#10;</div><div>Job Description&#10;</div><div>The Role and Impact&#10;</div><div>Intel is seeking a motivated and talented Silicon Architecture PhD Intern to join our team and contribute to the design and innovation of cutting-edge silicon solutions. In this role, you will have the opportunity to define and shape hardware, firmware, and platform specifications that drive the future of technology. As part of a collaborative and forward-thinking environment, you will assist in modeling and simulation, analyze performance, power, and feature trade-offs across subsystems, and influence architectural decisions to align with product goals. This is an exceptional opportunity to build skills, gain hands-on experience, and explore your career potential, all while supporting Intel's mission to deliver industry-leading solutions.&#10;</div><div>Key Responsibilities&#10;</div><div>- Contribute to the definition and architecture of silicon solutions, including hardware, firmware, and platform specifications.&#10;</div><div>- Assist in modeling and simulation to analyze subsystem performance, power, and feature trade-offs.&#10;</div><div>- Guide architectural decisions to ensure alignment with product goals and requirements.&#10;</div><div>- Collaborate with architects, design engineers, and validation teams to support feasibility studies and specification development.&#10;</div><div>- Engage in hands-on projects that support Intel's business goals and foster continuous learning and improvement.&#10;</div><div>Qualifications&#10;</div><div>Qualifications&#10;</div><div>Minimum Qualifications&#10;</div><div>- Proficiency in C/C++/C#.&#10;</div><div>- Strong knowledge of computer architecture, CPU architecture fundamentals, and microarchitecture fundamentals.&#10;</div><div>- Familiarity with SoC architecture and performance modeling techniques.&#10;<